cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Running Cogni-Brain (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) on NVIDIA DGX Spark with HashK GPU PLE and SGLang NEXTN"
message: "If you use this setup, benchmark wrappers, or HashK architecture, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rawat"
    given-names: "Rajendra Singh"
    affiliation: "cogni.chat"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5017-1341"
repository-code: "https://github.com/airawatraj/dgx-spark-qwen38-flash-agent"
abstract: >-
  A production-ready technical implementation and benchmarking suite for running
  RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 (~176B total params, 6B active) on a single
  NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10 Grace-Blackwell, 128 GB unified memory) served as Cogni-Brain
  in container spark-brain. By compressing the 51.2 GB n-gram PLE table 4x into a 12.8 GB
  GPU-resident HashK artifact, total resident weights fit in ~97 GB VRAM, unlocking
  NEXTN 3-step speculative decoding, FP8 KV caching with 700k+ token headroom, RadixAttention
  prefix caching up to 139,000 tok/s, and native agentic tool calling.
keywords:
  - "Qwen3.8-Flash-Next"
  - "Cogni-Brain"
  - "DGX Spark"
  - "GB10"
  - "Grace Blackwell"
  - "SGLang"
  - "HashK PLE"
  - "Speculative Decoding"
  - "NEXTN"
  - "MTP"
  - "AI Agents"
  - "NVFP4"
  - "Sparse Attention"
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-31"
